.TH BYTE_TRIML 3
.SH NAME
byte_triml \- remove leading characters from a byte array
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <byte.h>
.PP
.BI "const char* byte_triml(const char* " x ", size_t* " len ", const char* " charset ", unsigned int " charsetlen ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B byte_triml
scans the byte array
.I x
of length
.I *len
from left to right and skips any leading characters present in the provided
.I charset
(of length
.IR charsetlen ).
.PP
Upon returning, the function updates the value pointed to by
.I len
to reflect the number of bytes remaining after leading matches are removed, and returns a pointer to the start of the remaining byte sequence within the original buffer
.IR x .
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns a pointer to the first byte in the sequence that is not contained in
.I charset
. The variable pointed to by
.I len
is updated to the length of the resulting trimmed buffer.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR byte_trimr (3),
.BR byte_chr (3)